 # Desk profiles
 
-The document is {format:"profiles",items:{id:{rev:1,display:{theme,scale},paths:{home}}}}. Theme/home are strings (empty is valid); scale is a finite positive number. Each nested object has exactly the listed keys. Unsupported revisions, fields outside these sets and malformed fields are rejected. saveProfile replaces the matching id, keeps other profiles, and accepts flat {id,theme,scale,home} input. CLI set <id> <theme> <home> uses scale 1.
+The document is {format:"profiles",items:{id:{rev:2,display:{theme,scale},paths:{home},alerts:{muted}}}}. Theme/home are strings (empty is valid); scale is a finite positive number; muted is a boolean. Each nested object has exactly the listed keys. Unsupported revisions, fields outside these sets and malformed fields are rejected; legacy rev:1 records are read with alerts.muted set to false. saveProfile replaces the matching id, keeps other profiles, and accepts flat {id,theme,scale,home,alerts:{muted}} input; alerts.muted defaults to false. CLI set <id> <theme> <home> uses scale 1, and --muted sets alerts.muted to true.
 
 Run with Node.js. `npm test` runs the local checks.
 `node src/cli.js list` prints records and `node src/cli.js report` prints grouped counts.
